WEBVTT

00:00:20.830 --> 00:00:22.580
You'll be paired with me.

00:00:32.590 --> 00:00:34.590
Ichigo, you okay?

00:00:34.590 --> 00:00:37.470
It probably wouldn't help even if I said not to be nervous.

00:00:38.370 --> 00:00:41.510
You'll be on stage with <i>the</i> Kanzaki Mizuki after all.

00:00:42.620 --> 00:00:46.310
Ichigo-chan, no need to worry! I'm here for you.

00:00:46.310 --> 00:00:48.190
Are you trying to be Mizuki-san?

00:00:48.190 --> 00:00:49.410
You're way off.

00:00:49.410 --> 00:00:50.850
Come on...

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:54.560
It's a dream come true to be able to be on stage with Mizuki-chan!

00:00:56.250 --> 00:00:58.060
I'm way too excited!

00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:01.630
At least you're not getting stressed out.

00:01:01.630 --> 00:01:03.330
Yeah, that's our Ichigo.

00:01:03.330 --> 00:01:07.830
She was even able to pull off a Special Appeal at the entrance audition.

00:01:07.830 --> 00:01:11.050
I don't know whether she's got nerves of steel or is just dense.

00:01:11.050 --> 00:01:11.840
Ichigo.

00:01:13.400 --> 00:01:15.620
We're with you all the way.

00:01:15.620 --> 00:01:16.970
Thanks!

00:01:16.970 --> 00:01:19.550
I'll do my best to give a good performance.

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:20.770
Yeah.

00:01:27.060 --> 00:01:28.810
Here it is.

00:01:30.790 --> 00:01:32.070
Good mo—

00:01:42.420 --> 00:01:43.380
Mizuki-san.

00:01:43.380 --> 00:01:44.500
Hoshimiya.

00:02:04.900 --> 00:02:06.390
Hi, signalize!

00:02:06.530 --> 00:02:11.750
The answer lies on the other side of the sky

00:02:06.530 --> 00:02:11.750
kotae wa motto takai sora no kanata

00:02:11.980 --> 00:02:13.610
No, that's wrong

00:02:11.980 --> 00:02:13.610
iie chigau yo

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:18.990
I can see with my eyes that it's at the end of the Earth

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:18.990
boku no me ni mo mieta chi no hate

00:02:19.370 --> 00:02:20.780
Do that signalize!

00:02:20.910 --> 00:02:25.960
Something's starting to bubble up

00:02:20.910 --> 00:02:25.960
hageshiku natta mune no atsui powaa

00:02:26.250 --> 00:02:29.920
From the burning power in my raging heart

00:02:26.250 --> 00:02:29.920
sou da minagiru nanika ga

00:02:30.210 --> 00:02:33.460
So I'll believe in the present

00:02:30.210 --> 00:02:33.460
dakara ima wo shinjite

00:02:33.800 --> 00:02:38.630
And start today since it's more than a faint desire

00:02:33.800 --> 00:02:38.630
hajimeyou tada no akogare ja nai

00:02:38.680 --> 00:02:39.970
Chance for me

00:02:40.300 --> 00:02:45.270
Dreams can make even the harshest nightmare pleasant

00:02:40.300 --> 00:02:45.270
zankoku na yume ga yume de yume ni narunda

00:02:45.270 --> 00:02:49.480
It's just another challenge on the way

00:02:45.270 --> 00:02:49.480
hora chousen matteru yo

00:02:50.190 --> 00:02:54.400
Where are we headed?

00:02:50.190 --> 00:02:54.400
kimi to mukau basho wa doko darou

00:02:55.030 --> 00:02:58.150
Into a brilliant hope

00:02:55.030 --> 00:02:58.150
mabushii kibou no naka e

00:02:58.740 --> 00:03:05.410
Where do we want to go? Let's go find it right now

00:02:58.740 --> 00:03:05.410
nozomu basho wa doko darou sagashi ni ikou yo shuppatsu da

00:03:05.830 --> 00:03:08.790
Where we're headed

00:03:05.830 --> 00:03:08.790
mukau basho wa mirai no

00:03:09.580 --> 00:03:12.670
is into our hopes for the future

00:03:09.580 --> 00:03:12.670
bokura no kibou no naka ni

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:20.010
Our destination is the future, the light is our signal Let's go, go!

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:20.010
nozomu basho wa mirai no kagayaki ga aizu let's go, go

00:03:26.600 --> 00:03:30.270
Beautiful, wonderful morning, honeys!

00:03:31.210 --> 00:03:32.310
Oh yeah!

00:03:32.310 --> 00:03:36.440
Hoshimiya will be absent to prepare 
for the concert. Her seat's open.

00:03:36.940 --> 00:03:39.310
Good luck, Starmiya!

00:03:39.310 --> 00:03:41.950
And, showtime start.

00:03:42.360 --> 00:03:44.810
<i>If anyone can do it, it's Ichigo.</i>

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:46.700
Um...

00:03:47.050 --> 00:03:48.700
Aren't you going to greet everyone?

00:03:50.260 --> 00:03:53.040
Good morning! I look forward to working with you!

00:03:53.040 --> 00:03:55.080
Good morning.

00:03:55.080 --> 00:03:59.340
Good, good, that's what I want from a rookie. You've got spunk.

00:03:59.340 --> 00:04:01.090
You bet I do!

00:04:02.590 --> 00:04:04.470
She can make this work.

00:04:07.260 --> 00:04:09.350
Good morning.

00:04:09.350 --> 00:04:11.160
Hello, everyone.

00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:14.100
Is something wrong?

00:04:14.100 --> 00:04:15.950
No, nothing at all.

00:04:15.950 --> 00:04:18.350
Good morning, Headmistress.

00:04:18.350 --> 00:04:19.470
Good morning.

00:04:22.240 --> 00:04:25.740
Without further ado, let's begin the meeting.

00:04:26.340 --> 00:04:31.390
I, the Chief Manager Tsukikage, will now outline

00:04:31.390 --> 00:04:35.000
the plans for Mizuki Kanzaki's 
Premium Shiny Stage concert.

00:04:36.310 --> 00:04:38.300
We can accommodate 50,000 viewers.

00:04:38.300 --> 00:04:41.490
All 50,000 tickets for the Big Stadium show

00:04:41.490 --> 00:04:43.660
were sold out in just two seconds.

00:04:43.660 --> 00:04:44.580
Two seconds?!

00:04:45.510 --> 00:04:50.350
<i>So there really are </i>that<i> many people who want to see Mizuki-chan.</i>

00:04:50.350 --> 00:04:54.850
We will prepare various settings using the Aikatsu system to change stages on the fly.

00:04:54.850 --> 00:04:58.850
Within the stadium will we also be 
preparing a shop for Mizuki goods,

00:04:58.850 --> 00:05:02.440
a Mizuki Cafe for sweets made in her image,

00:05:02.440 --> 00:05:07.280
as well as a contest to determine who is most like Mizuki-chan.

00:05:07.280 --> 00:05:10.030
<i>Amazing. It's all centered around Mizuki-chan.</i>

00:05:10.540 --> 00:05:12.540
The performance will be two times longer than usual.

00:05:12.540 --> 00:05:14.540
We will have one thousand people on staff.

00:05:15.250 --> 00:05:20.550
Let us all work together to make this concert one that will forever be remembered in the history of idols.

00:05:20.550 --> 00:05:22.000
Understood!

00:05:22.410 --> 00:05:25.130
We will now proceed to introducing the performers.

00:05:25.130 --> 00:05:28.120
First up is our main event, Kanzaki Mizuki.

00:05:28.510 --> 00:05:30.050
I'm Kanzaki Mizuki.

00:05:30.050 --> 00:05:35.390
At this concert, I wish to surpass the limits that I have yet to break

00:05:35.390 --> 00:05:37.810
and show my fans a whole new Kanzaki Mizuki.

00:05:38.610 --> 00:05:40.290
I wish for your support.

00:05:41.820 --> 00:05:45.610
Next up is the rookie idol, Hoshimiya Ichigo.

00:05:45.610 --> 00:05:48.510
We plan for her to sing two songs.

00:05:48.510 --> 00:05:49.820
Hoshimiya.

00:05:49.820 --> 00:05:50.930
Yes!

00:05:53.950 --> 00:05:55.180
Introduce yourself.

00:05:55.800 --> 00:05:57.830
I-I'm sorry!

00:05:59.560 --> 00:06:01.960
Nice to meet you. My name is Hoshimiya Ichigo.

00:06:01.960 --> 00:06:04.670
Um... well...

00:06:04.670 --> 00:06:11.350
I may just be a first-year idol, but I promise to try my hardest not to lose to Mizuki-san! {not to disappoint?}

00:06:11.350 --> 00:06:13.200
I wish for your support.

00:06:13.800 --> 00:06:16.640
Excellent, she seems so fresh.

00:06:14.700 --> 00:06:16.490
We can do this!

00:06:18.550 --> 00:06:19.850
That was nerve-wracking.

00:06:19.850 --> 00:06:23.070
Moving along, I'd like to decide on the songs.

00:06:23.470 --> 00:06:26.490
Please look at the program placed in front of you.

00:06:27.360 --> 00:06:30.360
Is there anybody who holds an opinion about this?

00:06:31.370 --> 00:06:33.580
Mizuki, do you have any ideas?

00:06:33.580 --> 00:06:38.410
Yes. I want to start with a fun and happy song.

00:06:38.410 --> 00:06:40.890
There should be some sort of impact when I enter as well.

00:06:40.890 --> 00:06:45.650
For example, what about putting a small stage among the audience, and then entering from there?

00:06:45.650 --> 00:06:47.910
Sounds great, that's really interesting.

00:06:47.910 --> 00:06:50.120
Another good idea from Mizuki-chan. Let's go with that.

00:06:50.120 --> 00:06:53.800
Let's have a spotlight so that only Mizuki-chan is visible.

00:06:54.360 --> 00:06:55.920
It's getting better and better!

00:06:55.920 --> 00:06:57.570
Thank you very much.

00:06:58.440 --> 00:07:03.040
<i>Mizuki-chan's amazing for being able to talk to the adult staff members like this.</i>

00:07:04.020 --> 00:07:06.270
Good work, everyone.

00:07:05.000 --> 00:07:06.270
Good job.

00:07:08.100 --> 00:07:10.280
Good work, everybody.

00:07:12.390 --> 00:07:13.910
It's finally over.

00:07:14.240 --> 00:07:15.660
Hoshimiya, let's go.

00:07:15.660 --> 00:07:16.610
Huh?

00:07:19.290 --> 00:07:20.350
Yes!

00:07:27.970 --> 00:07:31.610
<i>Mizuki-chan always used to call me "Ichigo-chan"...</i>

00:07:31.610 --> 00:07:34.140
<i>I wonder why she starting using "Hoshimiya"?</i>

00:07:34.800 --> 00:07:36.940
I wonder if Ichigo's alright.

00:07:38.560 --> 00:07:40.560
It's Ichigo-tan!

00:07:40.560 --> 00:07:42.890
Are they going to the training room?

00:07:42.890 --> 00:07:44.470
Ichigo!

00:07:44.470 --> 00:07:47.020
Ichigo-tan!

00:07:48.030 --> 00:07:50.170
She left...

00:07:50.170 --> 00:07:53.710
It looked like she was in a hurry. Does she have more to do?

00:07:53.710 --> 00:07:56.200
Her "Training from Hell" is about to start.

00:07:56.790 --> 00:07:58.240
Tsukikage-san.

00:07:58.240 --> 00:07:59.580
It's been a while.

00:07:59.580 --> 00:08:01.720
"Training from Hell"?

00:08:01.720 --> 00:08:03.170
Sounds fun!

00:08:03.170 --> 00:08:05.580
Love you!

00:08:05.580 --> 00:08:08.570
Like doing 100 push-ups or 300 sit-ups.

00:08:08.570 --> 00:08:11.590
Maybe 1000 sprints or runway walking for 10,000 steps?

00:08:11.590 --> 00:08:13.520
It's nothing like that.

00:08:13.520 --> 00:08:16.600
When I say the "highlight of a concert", what do you think of?

00:08:17.970 --> 00:08:19.100
Ah!

00:08:36.320 --> 00:08:39.860
Amazing. She's doing the poses from when she does Cute Flash.

00:08:39.860 --> 00:08:42.960
So this is how Mizuki-san practices...

00:08:53.970 --> 00:08:55.970
Mizuki-san, you were wonderful.

00:08:55.970 --> 00:08:57.970
You're up next.

00:08:58.970 --> 00:09:02.890
It's time for your special training in order to bring out Special Appeals.

00:09:05.820 --> 00:09:07.200
O-Okay!

00:09:17.950 --> 00:09:29.590
Ai...katsu! Ai... katsu!

00:09:36.700 --> 00:09:39.600
I won't be able to use Special Appeals at this rate.

00:09:39.810 --> 00:09:43.090
Hoshimiya, do you understand what an appeal is?

00:09:43.930 --> 00:09:46.980
Yes... more or less.

00:09:46.980 --> 00:09:49.770
But I don't think I can explain it.

00:09:49.770 --> 00:09:56.330
An appeal is what we call the stage illusion that the Aikatsu system creates on stage.

00:09:56.330 --> 00:09:59.120
There are several different types of appeals.

00:09:59.880 --> 00:10:02.620
First is the Dress Appeal.

00:10:02.620 --> 00:10:05.120
Then the Type Special Appeal.

00:10:05.120 --> 00:10:10.430
Then we have one which can only be used when a single brand is used at once: the Brand Special Appeal.

00:10:10.430 --> 00:10:15.080
As the difficulty rises, you'll become able to use equivalently brilliant appeals.

00:10:15.080 --> 00:10:20.510
Finally, the most difficult one to pull off is the Premium Special Appeal.

00:10:21.300 --> 00:10:24.400
Special Appeals are the highlight of a show.

00:10:24.400 --> 00:10:27.470
They are the moment when your fans get the most fired up.

00:10:28.440 --> 00:10:32.520
You used a Special Appeal during
your entrance audition, am I right?

00:10:32.520 --> 00:10:33.880
Yes.

00:10:33.880 --> 00:10:35.910
Why do you think you were able to do it?

00:10:35.910 --> 00:10:37.280
"Why"?

00:10:37.930 --> 00:10:40.920
Back then, I was having so much fun.

00:10:40.920 --> 00:10:43.660
I thought that I wanted to continue it forever.

00:10:43.660 --> 00:10:45.860
And then, naturally...

00:10:45.860 --> 00:10:48.220
I believe that that's a wonderful thing.

00:10:48.870 --> 00:10:51.020
However, it was nothing more than chance.

00:10:51.750 --> 00:10:57.260
Only once you have mastered the Special Appeal and can use it on command can you be called a pro idol.

00:10:59.640 --> 00:11:04.010
Mizuki-san can already use Special Appeals the maximum three times.

00:11:04.010 --> 00:11:08.180
The only idol who can actually do that is Kanzaki Mizuki.

00:11:08.180 --> 00:11:13.400
And that's exactly why Kanzaki Mizuki is believed to be a true top idol nationwide.

00:11:14.530 --> 00:11:16.940
Ichigo-tan, fight on!

00:11:17.290 --> 00:11:22.240
But I'm just a rookie, it's impossible for me to be like you...

00:11:22.860 --> 00:11:24.200
And you're okay with that?

00:11:24.200 --> 00:11:25.330
What?

00:11:25.330 --> 00:11:30.210
It's certainly possible that people will let that pass if they know that you're new.

00:11:30.210 --> 00:11:32.710
But are you really okay with that?

00:11:34.210 --> 00:11:37.870
"I'm having fun, I want to continue this forever."

00:11:37.870 --> 00:11:41.500
Those feelings are very important for any idol.

00:11:42.220 --> 00:11:44.560
You already understand that well.

00:11:45.210 --> 00:11:49.810
However, to create a Special Appeal,
 there are other things you need.

00:11:49.810 --> 00:11:51.230
Like what?

00:11:52.700 --> 00:11:54.980
Mizuki, it's time.

00:11:55.430 --> 00:11:56.730
Okay!

00:11:57.130 --> 00:12:01.740
I've got a job lined up right now, so let's stop here for today.

00:12:01.740 --> 00:12:03.740
Um, Mizuki-san...

00:12:03.740 --> 00:12:05.240
Good work today.

00:12:10.150 --> 00:12:11.840
Something important...

00:12:16.670 --> 00:12:20.240
Ichigo's late... I wonder if she's still training?

00:12:24.570 --> 00:12:25.430
Yes.

00:12:26.590 --> 00:12:27.880
Tsukikage-san!

00:12:32.030 --> 00:12:33.120
<i>Ichigo...</i>

00:12:33.650 --> 00:12:44.140
Ai... katsu! Ai... katsu!

00:12:44.490 --> 00:12:47.000
Ai... katsu!

00:12:56.110 --> 00:12:57.040
Ichigo.

00:12:58.230 --> 00:12:59.840
Aoi, why are you here?

00:12:59.840 --> 00:13:02.210
Tsukikage-san gave me a call.

00:13:02.210 --> 00:13:06.450
She said that you were probably skipping dinner to keep training,

00:13:06.450 --> 00:13:08.720
and that I should come to get you.

00:13:12.190 --> 00:13:14.350
Come to think of it, I <i>am</i> hungry.

00:13:16.350 --> 00:13:17.480
Let's go back.

00:13:17.480 --> 00:13:18.370
Sure!

00:13:26.860 --> 00:13:28.730
Eat up and enjoy!

00:13:30.750 --> 00:13:32.620
Thanks for the food!

00:13:36.850 --> 00:13:38.250
It's great!

00:13:38.250 --> 00:13:40.650
Have you been training all this time?

00:13:40.650 --> 00:13:41.590
Yeah!

00:13:41.590 --> 00:13:43.470
You sure worked hard, Ichigo.

00:13:46.260 --> 00:13:48.680
Was the training really that difficult?

00:13:49.610 --> 00:13:50.930
It's not that...

00:13:50.930 --> 00:13:55.830
I wasn't able to do the Special Appeal poses at all.

00:13:55.830 --> 00:13:58.210
I just can't do it like Mizuki-chan...

00:13:58.210 --> 00:14:01.560
Of course it's impossible. Mizuki-chan is a top idol.

00:14:01.560 --> 00:14:04.030
You only became an idol very recently.

00:14:04.030 --> 00:14:05.820
That's not good enough.

00:14:06.780 --> 00:14:08.500
Mizuki-chan told me.

00:14:08.500 --> 00:14:12.910
She asked if I was alright with people overlooking my flaws just because I'm a rookie.

00:14:13.410 --> 00:14:16.410
But what <i>can</i> I do?

00:14:18.830 --> 00:14:21.080
Start by eating your omelette rice.

00:14:21.080 --> 00:14:23.170
I have something to show you afterwards.

00:14:26.350 --> 00:14:27.590
What are you doing?

00:14:27.590 --> 00:14:29.080
Give me a second.

00:14:30.340 --> 00:14:31.470
It's this.

00:14:31.470 --> 00:14:35.280
Oh, that's the Mizuki-chan fanclub's homepage.

00:14:35.280 --> 00:14:36.980
I visit the site sometimes too.

00:14:36.980 --> 00:14:39.480
There are comments from her fans here.

00:14:40.410 --> 00:14:42.480
"I want to see Mizuki-chan right now."

00:14:42.880 --> 00:14:46.240
"I'm sure your next concert will be the best you've ever had."

00:14:46.490 --> 00:14:50.240
"I'm looking forward to seeing the powered-up Mizuki-chan."

00:14:50.240 --> 00:14:53.240
Right, everyone's excited to see her.

00:14:53.240 --> 00:14:59.290
They buy their tickets months in advance and wait in anticipation for the day.

00:14:59.290 --> 00:15:03.210
Their expectations build up as they wonder what sort of concert they'll see.

00:15:03.210 --> 00:15:08.500
To her fans, the concerts are a time when they can be in the same place and spend the same time with Kanzaki Mizuki.

00:15:08.500 --> 00:15:10.660
It's an irreplaceable opportunity.

00:15:10.660 --> 00:15:14.780
It really gets your blood flowing to be able to hear your fans voices directly. {change of metaphor here}

00:15:14.780 --> 00:15:15.720
That's right.

00:15:15.720 --> 00:15:19.650
I can't be making any excuses by calling myself a newbie.

00:15:19.650 --> 00:15:20.980
Ran, thank you.

00:15:21.460 --> 00:15:23.730
I want everyone to enjoy the concert.

00:15:23.990 --> 00:15:28.070
That's why I'll give everything I've got to use three Special Appeals!

00:15:28.070 --> 00:15:29.350
You can do it!

00:15:34.780 --> 00:15:39.790
<i>I wonder what I should do to be able to use Special Appeals like Mizuki-chan.</i>

00:15:40.860 --> 00:15:46.030
<i>Having fun on the stage. Feeling 
like you want to continue it forever.</i>

00:15:46.030 --> 00:15:47.800
<i>And also...</i>

00:15:53.860 --> 00:15:58.350
<i>Mizuki-chan said that there were even more important things to keep in mind.</i>

00:15:59.230 --> 00:16:02.000
<i>But... what could they be?</i>

00:16:06.790 --> 00:16:08.890
Tomorrow's finally the performance.

00:16:08.890 --> 00:16:09.990
Right.

00:16:09.990 --> 00:16:12.950
You put in all of your effort.

00:16:12.950 --> 00:16:16.990
So during today's rehearsal, believe in yourself and give it everything you've got.

00:16:16.990 --> 00:16:17.990
I will.

00:16:19.080 --> 00:16:21.370
Um... Mizuki-san.

00:16:21.370 --> 00:16:22.370
Yes?

00:16:22.370 --> 00:16:26.440
Why did you suddenly start calling me "Hoshimiya"?

00:16:26.440 --> 00:16:29.880
You always used to call me "Ichigo-chan" before.

00:16:29.880 --> 00:16:34.240
It's because that's the proper way to address someone who can stand alongside you on stage.

00:16:34.240 --> 00:16:36.640
I want to face you head on.

00:16:38.650 --> 00:16:41.540
So you should come at me with the same determination.

00:16:41.540 --> 00:16:43.770
No holding back just because this is a rehearsal.

00:16:43.770 --> 00:16:44.720
Yes!

00:19:47.940 --> 00:19:51.960
I was only able to use a single Special Appeal...

00:19:52.540 --> 00:19:54.290
Good work!

00:19:55.460 --> 00:19:57.180
Good job, you two.

00:19:57.180 --> 00:19:59.550
Ichigo-chan, you were on the ball.

00:19:59.550 --> 00:20:03.310
You really <i>were</i> good. That was great for a beginner.

00:20:03.310 --> 00:20:05.140
Thank you very much.

00:20:05.140 --> 00:20:07.790
Be sure to do the same thing tomorrow.

00:20:07.790 --> 00:20:09.080
Y-Yes.

00:20:10.180 --> 00:20:12.980
But man, Mizuki-chan was awesome.

00:20:12.980 --> 00:20:17.440
She went all out even during the rehearsal. She even used three Special Appeals.

00:20:29.050 --> 00:20:30.640
Good work today.

00:20:31.910 --> 00:20:33.480
Good work.

00:20:38.980 --> 00:20:40.220
What's wrong?

00:20:40.800 --> 00:20:43.800
It's... nothing.

00:20:45.490 --> 00:20:48.700
Hoshimiya. I said not to hold back today.

00:20:55.540 --> 00:20:57.110
I'm so frustrated!

00:20:58.130 --> 00:21:01.760
I was only able to use one Special Appeal.

00:21:02.610 --> 00:21:08.070
I'm going to disappoint the people looking forward to tomorrow's concert.

00:21:13.980 --> 00:21:16.950
I'm sure you'll be able to use three tomorrow.

00:21:19.060 --> 00:21:23.280
You've already learned the most
 important feeling to hold, after all.

00:21:23.970 --> 00:21:26.970
But I... didn't do anything...

00:21:26.970 --> 00:21:29.870
Frustration at not being able to do something.

00:21:29.870 --> 00:21:30.610
Huh?

00:21:31.750 --> 00:21:33.980
With that, you'll be able to advance.

00:21:33.980 --> 00:21:38.280
Right. It's all over if you're satisfied with where you stand.

00:21:38.280 --> 00:21:41.150
But idols must be ever moving onwards.

00:21:42.520 --> 00:21:46.720
Even <i>you've</i> had times when you were frustrated at not being able to do something?

00:21:46.720 --> 00:21:49.420
Of course. I feel that everyday.

00:21:49.420 --> 00:21:52.720
That's why I always want to move forward.

00:21:58.300 --> 00:22:01.950
Amazing! You really are amazing!

00:22:01.950 --> 00:22:03.380
Hoshimiya...

00:22:03.380 --> 00:22:07.290
There's still one day left. I'm going to train until the very last minute!

00:22:07.290 --> 00:22:11.640
I want to use three Special Appeals and make everyone have the time of their life.

00:22:11.720 --> 00:22:14.770
I feel a faint potential from within that girl.

00:22:15.790 --> 00:22:17.350
An ability to draw others to her...

00:22:18.450 --> 00:22:20.930
<i>A natural-born...</i>

00:22:20.930 --> 00:22:22.100
<i>...star.</i>

00:23:55.690 --> 00:23:57.790
This week's Aikatsu Aphorism!

00:23:58.770 --> 00:24:01.680
There really <i>are</i> a lot of different types of Special Appeals, huh?

00:24:01.680 --> 00:24:03.730
Like flying into space, or floating like a butterfly!

00:24:03.730 --> 00:24:05.230
They're bright and fun!

00:24:05.230 --> 00:24:07.420
I've gotta practice too!

00:24:07.740 --> 00:24:09.920
Appeals are Flowers of the Stage!

00:24:10.780 --> 00:24:12.430
Only one day until the event.

00:24:12.430 --> 00:24:15.390
I've gotta give my all to not drag Mizuki-chan down!

00:24:15.390 --> 00:24:16.970
I'm going to move on too!

00:24:17.430 --> 00:24:18.900
Next time on Aikatsu!

00:24:18.900 --> 00:24:21.610
Heart Pounding!! Special Life: Part 2

00:24:21.610 --> 00:24:23.910
Always passionate, Idol Activities!
